    {
      "id": 493234,
      "username": "Lastie_Jason_Pule",
      "name": "Lastie Jason Pule",
      "created_at": "2026-02-03T14:57:22.223Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Hi <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/brian_pond\">@brian_pond</a>. Thank you for your response.</p>\n<p>Each person has their own ERPNext User account. They are not sharing the same user account.</p>\n<p>The issue occurs because they sometimes share the same physical workstation/browser. When User A logs out while on an inner page, and User B logs in on the same machine, User B is redirected to User A’s last visited page instead of starting at their own home page.</p>\n<p>So the problem is not shared credentials, but client-side state (route/session data) persisting across logouts on shared computers. The expected behavior is for every login to start fresh at the default home page, regardless of the previous user’s activity.</p>",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discuss.frappe.io/lastie_jason_pule/{size}/63803_2.png",
      "trust_level": 1,
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "like_count": null,
      "like_action": null,
      "Reads": 14,
